; tests/core-lexicon-band.fk — 64 self-defining words, eight query lanes, and
; twelve layers of query and response.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk ../control/offer-ack-core.fk form-stdlib/core-lexicon.fk
;
; Verdict 262143 — eighteen readings at POWERS OF TWO. The first cut of this
; fold used powers of ten, reached 10^17, and diverged: Go, Rust and fkwu said
; 111111111111111111 while TypeScript said 111111111111111120. Every scalar
; underneath was identical on all four arms; only the encoding broke, because
; 10^17 is past 2^53, the largest integer a JavaScript double carries exactly.
; Bits keep it at 262143 — the same choice homecoming-distillation-corpus-band's
; 8191 already makes.
;
; On Go / Rust / TypeScript / fkwu:
;   the lexicon holds exactly 64 words, 8 families of 8                        1
;   CLOSED UNDER DEFINITION — every token of every defining sentence is
;     one of the 64 or one of the named glue words; nothing borrowed           2
;   494 definition tokens carry it                                             4
;   exactly ONE of the eight lanes can answer with a terminal ack              8
;   and it is `whether` — the only lane that asks for a truth rather than
;     a thing, which is why it is the only one that can end a conversation     16
;   asking whether of any word rests at layer 1                                32
;   EVERY one of the 64 why-chains bottoms out within 8 layers                 64
;   the deepest is exactly 8 — the walk from the far family to the ground      128
;   and every why-chain rests in NOTHING, never in 1: no floor under the
;     floor, and a chain ending in 1 would be a self-grounding claim           256
;   `what` settles on `thing` at layer 2 and never moves again                 512
;   `which` is still a live node at layer 12                                   1024
;   and it cycles with period 8 — the family ring                              2048
;   `nothing` is reached for by other definitions; `whether` is a word
;     here and `maybe` is not                                                  4096
;   the spacing holds: kind sits at 7007, nothing at 0                         8192
;   CLOSED UNDER QUESTIONING — no lane answers with anything outside the
;     64; you cannot ask your way out of this vocabulary                       16384
;   exactly one lane is REVERSIBLE (`which`), and `what` is not                32768
;   the collapse is measured, not asserted: which keeps all 64 answers,
;     whether keeps 2, what keeps 1                                            65536
;   THE LAW — across all eight lanes, reversible holds exactly when every
;     chain returns to where it started. A step that loses nothing can be
;     walked backwards, so it imposes no order and no time; a step that
;     collapses two words onto one cannot be undone, and that missing
;     distinction is the condition, the one-way direction the separation.
;     `what` is why "never rests" will not do as the test: it collapses
;     onto `thing`, a fixed point that is still a NODE, so the chain runs
;     forever and yet nothing can be recovered. Returning is the test.       131072

(do
    (cl-check))
